## 2. Hello prints check FILE Nms

  Cwd: `/home/jeryd/.grok/worktrees/ooda-cli-three`
  Command:

    ./bin/ooda bench fixtures/hello.oo

  Grammar: prefix `ooda bench: check`, then FILE, then N, then `ms`.
  N is a decimal integer. N >= 0. Letters `ms` have no space.

  Pass 1 (`bench_hello.log`):
    `OK`
    `ooda bench: check fixtures/hello.oo 5ms`
    EXIT 0

  Pass 2 (`bench_hello_run2.log`):
    `OK`
    `ooda bench: check fixtures/hello.oo 6ms`
    EXIT 0

  Smoke cache (same Combined binary, `scripts/bench_smoke.oo`):
    `.ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/bench_smoke/hello.out`
    `ooda bench: check fixtures/hello.oo 21ms`

  Times 5, 6, and 21 differ. All parse as integer milliseconds >= 0.
  Check child may print `OK`. That is the compiler. It is not
  `ooda bench: ok`.

  `./bin/ooda run ./scripts/bench_smoke.oo` prints
  `bench_smoke: PASSED` and exits 0 (`bench_smoke.log`).

