  Missing file:

    ./bin/ooda bench missing_no_such.oo

  stdout: `ERR<TAB>bench<TAB>unreadable file: missing_no_such.oo`
  stderr: empty
  EXIT_MISS: 2
  No check line. No `ooda bench: ok`.

  Log: `/tmp/grok-goal-e3250e659225/implementer/bench_bad.log`
  Combined smoke cache has the same two stdout lines
  (`none.out`, `miss.out`).

  Same refuse, same exit 2, same usage, no ok:

    ./bin/ooda bench --run
    ./bin/ooda bench --run --run

  `--run` is a flag. It is not a path.

  On disk (`cli/cmd_more.oo`) and in Combined C emit:

    path == ""            -> usage; `oo_process_exit(2)`
    file not on disk      -> ERR unreadable; `oo_process_exit(2)`

  Check fail is exit 1. That is not a bad-arg case.

